Step 2 — Don't create a separate listener class yet

I would first use Reactor's built-in retry hook.

Your existing method probably looks something like:

public Retry createRetry(int maxAttempts, long initialDelaySeconds) {
    return Retry.backoff(maxAttempts, Duration.ofSeconds(initialDelaySeconds))
        .filter(this::isRetryable)
        .onRetryExhaustedThrow((retryBackoffSpec, retrySignal) ->
            new RuntimeException(
                "Retries exhausted for the request",
                retrySignal.failure()
            )
        );
}

Add the logging hook to this existing configuration.

The flow becomes:

Exception
   ↓
isRetryable()
   ↓
RetryBackoffSpec
   ↓
doBeforeRetry()
   ↓
LOG exception + attempt
   ↓
backoff
   ↓
retry

Reactor specifically documents doBeforeRetry() and doAfterRetry() for side effects around retry triggers. 


