Step 6 — Improve onRetryExhaustedThrow()

You already have:

.onRetryExhaustedThrow((retryBackoffSpec, retrySignal) ->
    new RuntimeException(
        "Retries exhausted for the request",
        retrySignal.failure()
    )
)

You can also log here if you want a final/exhausted retry log.

That gives you:

Attempt 1 → log
Attempt 2 → log
Attempt 3 → log
Retries exhausted → log final failure

However, don't blindly log the same exception twice. Decide whether your team's logging standard wants:

Option A — only each retry

Retry attempt 1
Retry attempt 2
Retry attempt 3

or

Option B — retry attempts + final exhaustion

Retry attempt 1
Retry attempt 2
Retry attempt 3
Retries exhausted

For production troubleshooting, I'd lean toward B, provided the logs aren't duplicated elsewhere.


