Step 11 — Use StepVerifier if the retry is reactive

If your WebClient method returns Mono/Flux, StepVerifier is a good way to test the behavior.

For example, conceptually:

StepVerifier.create(
    failingMono.retryWhen(retryConfig.createRetry(3, 1))
)
.expectError()
.verify();

You can also count how many times the source was subscribed/invoked using an AtomicInteger.

Reactor provides retryWhen specifically for applying a Retry strategy to a reactive sequence. 


