Since your code is using:

RetryBackoffSpec
RetrySignal

I would not implement a custom Spring-style RetryListener unless your team specifically requires a separate listener abstraction.

Reactor already provides the equivalent hook:

RetryBackoffSpec
    .doBeforeRetry(...)
    .doAfterRetry(...)

and the official Reactor documentation explicitly describes these hooks as being useful for retry-side effects such as logging. 

So your proposed architecture can simply be:

